Z||000000||Austin||09-14-2001||12:20 AM||||I have some concerns.  I just replaced my heater core cause like most people, foggy windshields and floor soaked with antifreeze are not very attractive.<P>I never really used my heat but I did after I changed cores.  I have noticed that that when I use the heat as oppossed to a/c (my car does have a/c by the way) the air doesn't blow as well.  Hopefully that is in my head but I'm not too sure.  <P>Also, I have another concern.  When I do use my heat, I think my performance is affected slighty.  I'm not too sure if the same thing happens when I use the a/c.  Should be car run and accelerate slower when the heat is on?  It should also be noted that my low coolant light has come off and on the last 10 I've driven my car (I'm getting coolant first thing in the morning).  Is it possible I unhooked a harness or something when I changed heater cores?  <P>Somebody help!!!||||reg||4
Z||000001||Phil||09-14-2001||04:59 PM||||The most likely cause of the heater not seeming to "blow" as hard as the AC is that the heater vents exit the bottom down near the foot wells, whereas the AC blows right into your puss. As for the overheating you may have gotten a air bubble in the cooling system. Follow the procedure for burping the cooling system.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
